1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:04,639
I need a bracket that holds a stepper motor on an aluminium extrusion.

2
00:00:04,639 --> 00:00:07,560
Bent from sheet metal, and cut by a laser service.

3
00:00:08,510 --> 00:00:12,000
Today I'll show you how to design it without any CAD knowledge.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,760
SOMA AI builds the bracket around the real motor and extrusion, and unfolds it into a DXF for the laser.

5
00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:21,508
We use SOMA.

6
00:00:21,508 --> 00:00:25,680
It's free and open source, and you can download it at somacad.app.

7
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:28,154
SOMA itself is free.

8
00:00:28,154 --> 00:00:30,821
For SOMA AI, you bring your own AI:

9
00:00:30,821 --> 00:00:33,640
a ChatGPT subscription or an API key.

10
00:00:35,350 --> 00:00:38,400
I start a new model and import two STEP files:

11
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:42,908
a NEMA 17 stepper motor and a 100 mm piece of 2020 V-slot extrusion.

12
00:00:42,908 --> 00:00:47,880
Both come from the FreeCAD parts library, under a Creative Commons license.

13
00:00:50,817 --> 00:00:53,961
You can view the STEP files by clicking them in the file browser.

14
00:00:53,961 --> 00:00:55,267
They show up in the viewer.

15
00:00:57,783 --> 00:01:01,193
The files sit in the inputs folder, where SOMA AI can use them.

16
00:01:05,517 --> 00:01:07,931
Skills tell SOMA AI how your parts are made.

17
00:01:07,931 --> 00:01:12,047
There's one for sheet metal, and also for laser cutting and plasma cutting.

18
00:01:15,484 --> 00:01:18,250
I set the sheet metal skill to my material:

19
00:01:18,250 --> 00:01:20,951
2 mm steel, with a 2 mm inner bend radius.

20
00:01:20,951 --> 00:01:22,945
SOMA AI then follows its rules:

21
00:01:22,945 --> 00:01:28,734
distances from holes to bends, bend reliefs, and the flat pattern with the right K-factor.

22
00:01:33,050 --> 00:01:35,171
Everything is prepared.

23
00:01:35,171 --> 00:01:38,674
Now we build the bracket with SOMA AI.

24
00:01:38,674 --> 00:01:41,994
I click its tab, and pick the model:

25
00:01:41,994 --> 00:01:43,100
GPT-6.1 Sol.

26
00:01:50,817 --> 00:01:53,151
I describe what I need in plain words:

27
00:01:53,151 --> 00:02:00,707
the motor at the end of the extrusion, the shaft sideways for a belt, slots to tension the belt, and M5 screws with T-nuts.

28
00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:08,064
Before it starts, SOMA AI asks what is still open.

29
00:02:08,064 --> 00:02:10,120
I click my answers and send them.

30
00:02:13,317 --> 00:02:19,442
Then it measures the motor and the extrusion in the STEP files, picks the screws, and builds the bracket.

31
00:02:19,442 --> 00:02:21,367
SOMA shows every step right away.

32
00:02:22,317 --> 00:02:22,917
Here it is.

33
00:02:22,917 --> 00:02:28,367
The structure tree lists the bracket and the screws, with the motor and the extrusion as references.

34
00:02:29,717 --> 00:02:30,989
It's a C-shaped channel:

35
00:02:30,989 --> 00:02:35,494
a plate that carries the motor, with a flange bent back along the top and the bottom.

36
00:02:35,494 --> 00:02:38,727
The motor sits in slots, so it can slide to tension the belt.

37
00:02:40,484 --> 00:02:42,724
From behind, you see how the motor is held:

38
00:02:42,724 --> 00:02:46,997
four screws with washers in the slots, and the shaft comes through for the pulley.

39
00:02:51,150 --> 00:02:54,723
To look at the model, SOMA has viewing tools that change nothing.

40
00:02:54,723 --> 00:02:59,120
Explode pulls the bracket and its screws apart, so you see how they go together.

41
00:03:05,417 --> 00:03:07,358
And a section cuts through the middle:

42
00:03:07,358 --> 00:03:11,547
the two bends with their radius, and the screws going into the T-nuts in the slot.

43
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:17,510
Now the file for the laser service.

44
00:03:17,510 --> 00:03:24,082
I ask for the flat pattern as a DXF, with the bend lines on their own layer, and a drawing with a bend table.

45
00:03:29,633 --> 00:03:31,339
SOMA AI unfolds the bracket.

46
00:03:31,339 --> 00:03:36,883
Each bend adds a little length, worked out from the radius, the thickness and the K-factor.

47
00:03:38,833 --> 00:03:41,492
Click the DXF, and SOMA opens it right here:

48
00:03:41,492 --> 00:03:45,601
the outline and holes to cut, and the bend lines on their own layer.

49
00:03:52,367 --> 00:03:53,315
And the drawing:

50
00:03:53,315 --> 00:03:58,705
the flat blank with its size, and a table with every bend, its direction, angle and radius.

51
00:04:04,066 --> 00:04:04,930
One more thing:

52
00:04:04,930 --> 00:04:07,753
a limit switch, so the carriage stops at the end.

53
00:04:07,753 --> 00:04:11,556
I import a real micro switch, also from the FreeCAD parts library.

54
00:04:16,366 --> 00:04:20,096
With Mark up, I simply draw where I want it, and write what it is.

55
00:04:21,366 --> 00:04:24,456
A circle where the tab should go, an arrow, and a short note.

56
00:04:32,033 --> 00:04:34,643
Send it to SOMA AI, and add one sentence.

57
00:04:35,666 --> 00:04:39,607
The switch lever should face the carriage, so the carriage presses it at the end of travel.

58
00:04:47,199 --> 00:04:53,284
There's the tab, bent up from the top flange, with the micro switch screwed on and its lever facing the carriage.

59
00:04:53,284 --> 00:04:55,169
And the flat pattern grows with it.

60
00:04:58,733 --> 00:05:01,543
SOMA AI also made the main sizes adjustable.

61
00:05:01,543 --> 00:05:05,183
In the Parameters tab, I change the sheet from 2 to 3 mm.

62
00:05:06,933 --> 00:05:11,383
A moment later the bracket is thicker, and the flat pattern has the new bend allowance.

63
00:05:13,133 --> 00:05:15,705
Open the DXF again, and it's up to date.

64
00:05:15,705 --> 00:05:16,863
Ready to send off.

65
00:05:20,266 --> 00:05:24,324
Upload it to a laser cutting service, bend the flanges, and bolt the motor on.

66
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:28,382
And if you cut your own parts on a plasma table, there's a skill for that too.

67
00:05:30,133 --> 00:05:35,149
From two STEP files to a flat pattern for the laser, without drawing a single line.

68
00:05:35,149 --> 00:05:37,143
Get SOMA for free at somacad.app.
